================================================================================
Third-party components vendored / statically linked into release binaries
================================================================================

The following third-party components are vendored into this repository and
may be statically compiled into release artifacts. Their original license
texts are preserved verbatim alongside the source code. End users distributing
xClaw binaries MUST also distribute or otherwise make available the license
texts and (where the license requires it) the corresponding component source.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. bubblewrap — LGPL-2.0-or-later
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:        https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap
Upstream version: 0.11.0 (see crates/vendor/bubblewrap/NEWS.md and meson.build)
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.0-or-later
   (declared in the SPDX header of every C/H source file, e.g.
    crates/vendor/bubblewrap/bubblewrap.c line 3)
License texts:   crates/vendor/bubblewrap/COPYING
                 crates/vendor/bubblewrap/LICENSE
Vendored path:   crates/vendor/bubblewrap/
                 (byte-for-byte mirror of
                  codex-cli-main/codex-rs/vendor/bubblewrap/, per ADR-129 §1.3
                  verbatim-port red line; this path is a sibling of the
                  consuming crate `crates/dasclaw_sandbox_linux/` to mirror
                  upstream codex's `codex-rs/vendor/` sibling layout, which
                  matches the relative path `../vendor/bubblewrap` referenced
                  from `crates/dasclaw_sandbox_linux/build.rs` line 16; see
                  ADR-144 §6 OQ-C1c-7 and the Wave-C1c P1.1 PR for layout
                  rationale)
Use in release:  The C sources (bubblewrap.c, bind-mount.c, network.c,
                 utils.c) are statically linked into the
                 `dasclaw_sandbox_linux` crate's release binary on Linux via
                 the crate's build.rs (after Wave-C1c Phase 1.1 lands; see
                 ADR-144). Until Phase 1.1 ships, the sources are present in
                 the tree but not yet compiled into any artifact.

LGPL §6 compliance posture: xClaw distributes the complete corresponding
source for bubblewrap in this repository under
`crates/vendor/bubblewrap/`, including unmodified
COPYING/LICENSE files and the unmodified C source. Building xClaw from source
re-links bubblewrap automatically. This satisfies LGPL-2.0-or-later §6(a)
(distribute complete corresponding source) for source-form distributions.
For binary distributions, downstream packagers MUST additionally provide a
mechanism allowing the recipient to combine modified bubblewrap sources with
the rest of the binary (LGPL §6(b) "object code + relinking instructions"
or §6(c) "written offer to supply source"). See PR description for the
project-level legal sign-off and the chosen §6 mechanism.

